[#:seon.task{:name "the-cache-sits-at-its-byte-budget-during-check-runs"
             :plan "In the projections lane's `bin/seon check` JVMs (2026-10-14), `seon.cache` sat at its 512 MB budget: after a 22-value `d/with` batch, `:seon.db/value-projection` alone held 44 entries, about 474 MB, and the next registration write took about 2x its time before the batch (HEAD 46.7 to 110.5 ms, median of 7). Speculative projections are retained like committed ones, then evicted. The deferred phase 2 of `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/truths-hybrid.md` owns it: a speculative projection held only for its operation. Re-measure once phase 2 lands. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/cache-after-boot.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/proj-content-key-2.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "one-weighted-cache-under-a-memory-cap"
